      "notes": "Serum PK parameters given in the Fig. 1 legend, neutropenic infected mice\nS02 | DOI 10.1128/AAC.47.10.3165-3169.2003 | Fig. 1 legend and Results text (Andes et al. 2003)\nFemale ICR/Swiss mice 23-27 g, neutropenic (cyclophosphamide 150 mg/kg day -4, 100 mg/kg day -1), infected (disseminated candidiasis). Single ORAL GAVAGE 10, 20, 40 mg/kg; retro-orbital SERUM, 3 mice per time, every 1-2 h over 5 h; microbiological agar-well assay (Candida kefyr), detection limit 0.25 µg/ml; at 10 mg/kg only 2 time points were above the limit.\nConcentration-time points are in Fig. 1 only (geometric mean ± SD of 3 mice; not digitized). Values below are transcribed from the legend text, not read from the plot.\nResults text: \"The elimination half-life ranged from 0.72 to 2.9 h.\" (legend gives 0.68 h at 10 mg/kg). Protein binding: \"The level of protein binding in mouse serum was 78% at concentrations of 10 and 100 μg/ml.\"",
